## Summary
The Italian Supervisory Authority imposed a total fine of €11.5 million on Eni Gas e Luce for violating the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). The fines were announced on January 17, 2020, and consisted of two separate amounts: €8.5 million and €3 million.

## Key Points
- Eni Gas e Luce received a total fine of €11.5 million from the Italian Supervisory Authority.
- The fines were imposed for multiple violations of the GDPR.
- The fines were split into two separate amounts: €8.5 million and €3 million.
- The announcement of the fines was made on January 17, 2020.


